# Research Library Issues: A Report from ARL, CNI, and SPARC. RLI 284

**Authors:** Baughman, M. Sue, Ed.

## Abstract
&quot;Research Library Issues&quot; (&quot;RLI&quot;) focuses on current and emerging topics that are strategically important to research libraries. The articles explore issues, share information, pose critical questions, and provide examples. This issue includes the following articles: (1) Introduction (Sue Baughman); (2) An Overview of the Digital Humanities (Donald J. Waters); and (3) Library Space Assessment: Focusing on Learning (Joan K. Lippincott and Kim Duckett). Individual articles contain endnotes.

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=ED583577

